WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.013
Two limits.

2
00:00:01.013 --> 00:00:03.062
First, what the scan can't see.

3
00:00:03.062 --> 00:00:06.337
For synced users, a write
made in Active Directory

4
00:00:06.337 --> 00:00:09.612
never reaches the Entra
audit log this scan reads.

5
00:00:09.612 --> 00:00:12.813
Only Active Directory's own
change auditing sees it.

6
00:00:12.813 --> 00:00:17.395
The guide's interim path covers that:
it names the sync agent as a writer in

7
00:00:17.395 --> 00:00:22.437
the register, and reviews the access
control lists on the organizational units.

8
00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:24.763
Second, what the scan can't confirm.

9
00:00:24.763 --> 00:00:29.562
To match an Update user record, the
register names the property that changed.

10
00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:33.924
Learn doesn't document those names,
so each one is the program's reading.

11
00:00:33.924 --> 00:00:37.513
If a name is wrong, the scan
reports nothing for that value,

12
00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:40.337
and silence looks exactly
like a clean month.

13
00:00:40.337 --> 00:00:43.712
That's why Lab 2 matters more
here than in most modules.

14
00:00:43.712 --> 00:00:46.430
Confirm every property name against a real

15
00:00:46.430 --> 00:00:49.510
audit record before the
scan counts as evidence.
